{
  "dom_id": "step-q221392",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Let $t$ be a prime number. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. If $11∣t$ then $t=11$\n\nII. If $t\\,|\\,2$ then $t=2$\n\nIII. If $t\\,|\\,44$ then $t=11$",
  "worked_solution": "For any prime numbers $t$ and $s,$\n\n$t∣s\\,\\text{or}\\,s∣t\\,⟹\\,t=s.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. As $11$ and $t$ are prime numbers and $11∣t,$ we must have $t=11.$\n\n- Statement II is true. As $t$ and $2$ are prime numbers and $t∣2,$ we must have $t=2.$\n\n- Statement III is false. As a counterexample, let $t=2.$ Then, $2∣44$ but $2\\ne 11.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
